# Dev model for B17 (checklist 0.6), with a context window big enough for a stat card.
#
# qwen2.5:7b-instruct ships with no num_ctx of its own, so Ollama applies its
# default of 2048. A stat card with 12 anchors plus the target question runs to
# ~1,300 tokens and grows; llama.cpp truncates the OLDEST tokens silently, and
# the oldest tokens are the top of the card — the cluster definition. Every
# cluster would then look identical to the model, which is indistinguishable in
# the output from F2, the failure the spec calls the most likely way this
# project fails while looking like it works.
#
# The base model supports 32768. 8192 is chosen over the maximum because the KV
# cache is resident RAM on a 16 GB machine that is also running the pipeline,
# and 8192 is 6x the largest prompt the design produces.
#
#   ollama create qwen2.5-ctx8k:7b-instruct-8192 -f Modelfile
#
# The tag is explicit on purpose. A locally created model with a bare name
# resolves to :latest, which moves if the model is ever rebuilt differently —
# and cache.py keys responses on the model string, so two sets of weights would
# share one cache key and a resumed run would mix them into one ensemble. The
# tag names the base and the window, so rebuilding with a different window
# produces a different key rather than a silent collision.
FROM qwen2.5:7b-instruct
PARAMETER num_ctx 8192
